#
# Patchlevel: Xservers_1.3
#
# Xservers file, workstation prototype
#
# This file should contain an entry to start the server on the
# local display; if you have more than one display (not screen),
# you can add entries to the list (one per line).  If you also
# have some X terminals connected which do not support XDMCP,
# you can add them here as well.  Each X terminal line should
# look like:
#	XTerminalName:0 foreign
#
# Uncomment ONLY ONE line per SCREEN_GROUP below.
# The SCREEN_GROUP number is the ALT-Function Key number for the display.
#
# Since the Amiga has multiple displays, you need to be circumspect in
# your choice of display number.  Especially refrain from using :0 as
# the display number.  :0 is the display number used if a user simply
# types X.  If you use :0 for XDM, that user's X will NOT work unless
# they explicitly set DISPLAY in the environment.  The screen group makes
# an excellent choice for the display number.
#
#
# INSTRUCTIONS FOR CONFIGURATION OF THIS FILE:
#
# The amixadm script ONLY handles xdm on Alt-F10.
# You should uncomment only ONE of the executable lines below.
# To use a different window manager, edit the .xsession file in 
# the user's home directory.
#
# ALT-F10, and SCREEN_GROUP 10 ARE THE DEFAULTS.
#
# NOTE: a trailing :10 means that X will run as DISPLAY=hostname:10.0
#
#
# A2410 card at 1024x768:
#:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X -tiga :10
#
# A2410 card at 800x600:
#:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X -tiga -tm 3 :10
#
# DMI Resolver card at 800x600:
#:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X -res -tm 0 :10
#
# DMI Resolver card at 1024x768:
#:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X -res -tm 2 :10
#
# DMI Resolver card at 1280x1024:
#:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X -res -tm 3 :10
#
# Monochrome X: 1024x768 on A2024 or Moniterm, 640x480 on other monitors
:10 local /usr/bin/env SCREEN_GROUP=10 /usr/bin/X11/X :10
